          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On February 4, 2012, around 23:15, individuals located in Yvelines and Aube witnessed in the sky the silent movement of a luminous phenomenon with blue-green and orange colors. The trajectory was straight. The testimonies closely match the characteristics of an atmospheric reentry observation. The direction towards West-Southwest and the duration of only a few seconds rule out the hypothesis of a reentry of space debris. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable atmospheric reentry of a meteoroid (meteorite fall).",
